## Layout
- `code/` — the code repository (this is where Claude Code is launched).
- `../docs/` — project wiki. Start with `../docs/INDEX.md` (one line per page).
- `../.claude/rules/` — detailed rules scoped with `paths:`.
- Docs live in the private `{{CORE_NAME}}` repo; code lives in its own repo.

## Rules
- Write all code, comments and Markdown in English. Talk to the user in their language
  (from their Claude settings or instructions; otherwise the language they write in).
- After each working step run `save "<message>"` (commits code and docs together).
  To undo a step: `undo-step`. To publish: `save "<message>" --push`.
  Both commands live in `{{CORE_DIR}}/bin/`.
- After changing a feature, update its page in `../docs/features/` and its `updated` field.
- A new architectural decision gets a new file `../docs/decisions/NNN-<slug>.md`.
- Put specs and plans (e.g. from Superpowers) in `../docs/superpowers/`, not in `code/`.
- Never edit `../docs/` from a worktree under `code/.claude/worktrees/`; the main session
  updates docs after merging.
- Never read `.env` files or `~/.ssh`.
